% You are an expert TypeScript engineer. Implement the SiteVelocity persistence repository boundary.

<include>prompts/context/sitevelocity-preamble.prompt</include>
<include>prompts/context/domain-types.prompt</include>

<pdd-reason>Persist authoritative domain records and immutable research snapshots without leaking Supabase types into application code.</pdd-reason>

<pdd-interface>
{"type":"module","module":{"functions":[{"name":"createPersistenceRepository","signature":"(client: PersistenceClient, clock: Clock) -> PersistenceRepository","returns":"PersistenceRepository"}]}}
</pdd-interface>

<responsibility>
Provide a provider-neutral repository for candidates, sites, evidence, findings, agent runs, snapshots, and command receipts with deterministic mapping and explicit missing/conflict results.
</responsibility>

<non_responsibilities>
- DOES NOT call research, model, workflow, or government-data providers.
- DOES NOT calculate scores, infer facts, or rewrite evidence.
- MUST NOT expose database, Supabase, SQL, or transport types through the public interface.
- MUST NOT place privileged credentials in browser-reachable code or results.
</non_responsibilities>

<vocabulary>
repository record: a plain domain value accepted or returned by this module.
immutable snapshot: a research snapshot whose content cannot be updated after insertion.
command receipt: the stored result associated with one idempotency command identifier.
conflict: an attempted insert whose stable identifier already exists with different content.
missing: no matching record exists; it is not an empty or negative factual conclusion.
safe retry: a later attempt using the same unchanged records and a new permitted transaction attempt.
</vocabulary>

<contract_rules>
R1 (MUST): Return only plain JSON-serializable domain values and stable repository result unions.
R2 (MUST): Preserve source identifiers, provenance, evidence links, finding status, timestamps supplied by the caller, and snapshot version exactly.
R3 (MUST): Insert a research snapshot once and reject any later mutation or different-content replacement under the same snapshot identifier.
R4 (MUST): Store a command receipt atomically with its result and return the stored result for an identical repeated command identifier.
R5 (MUST): Report different-input reuse of a command identifier as conflict and perform no write.
R6 (MUST): Distinguish missing, stored, and conflict results; missing never becomes an empty domain record.
R7 (MUST): Apply multi-record writes atomically so partial evidence, findings, agent runs, or snapshot state is never visible.
R8 (MUST NOT): Return secret values, database connection details, raw SQL errors, or provider client objects in results or diagnostics.
R9 (MUST): Convert storage failures into stable sanitized failure codes while retaining the original records unchanged for a safe retry.
R10 (MUST): Produce structurally identical mappings for structurally identical storage rows and never consult randomness.
</contract_rules>

<deliverables>
Generate `lib/persistence/repository.ts`. Export the repository interfaces, stable result unions, and `createPersistenceRepository`. Keep the concrete Supabase client behind the declared `PersistenceClient` port.
</deliverables>
